.TH SDL_stack_free 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_stack_free \- Free memory previously allocated with
.BR SDL_stack_alloc .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_stack_free(data) ((void)(data))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If SDL used alloca() to allocate this memory, this macro does nothing (other than insert
.BR ((void)(data)
so the compiler sees an expression) and the allocated memory will be automatically released when the function that called
.BR SDL_stack_alloc ()
returns\[char46] If SDL used
.BR SDL_malloc (),
it will
.BR SDL_free
the memory immediately\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I data
the pointer, from
.BR SDL_stack_alloc (),
to free\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_stack_alloc (3)
